---
intent: >
  Extend provisionBrain's bundled brain.aide template, return-shape, step-list,
  and tests from the current 3-section / 5-step / 2-artifact contract to the
  amended 4-section / 6-step / 3-artifact contract. Adds the studyPlaybook body
  section to obsidianBrainAideTemplate (sourced verbatim from the
  multi-month-tested skill prose at .claude/skills/study-playbook/SKILL.md),
  trims the playbook section to pure conventions, extends resolveBrainAideBody
  to return { playbook, studyPlaybook, research }, inserts buildStudyPlaybookStep
  between buildPlaybookStep and buildResearchStep (presence-only idempotency at
  brain-relative path coding-playbook/study-playbook.md), and updates both test
  files. Existing tests remain green; new tests cover the new section/step/artifact.
---

## Project Structure

After this plan executes, the `provisionBrain/` module looks like this. The
folder is the same scope directory this plan.aide lives in. `[E]` marks files
that already exist and are modified by this plan; `[E*]` marks the only file
unchanged structurally but with bytes that round-trip differently because it
participates in the new four-section grammar (none in this plan); `[NEW]`
marks files that did not exist before this plan ran. There are NO new files
in this plan — every change is an in-place edit to an existing file. The
new builder lives inline in `index.ts`, mirroring the existing
`buildPlaybookStep` and `buildResearchStep` siblings.

```
